<%# File: views/content/admin-income-report.ejs
    Purpose: Payment Collection — one row per transaction.

    RENAMED FROM "INCOME REPORT" (Phase 7.3)
    This page reports money COLLECTED from students. It says nothing about what
    the centre spends, so calling it income invited staff to read it as a profit
    figure. The URL is still /income-report: old links and bookmarks resolve.

    WHAT WENT (Phase 7.3)
    The "Monthly income" and "Income per branch" charts, and the whole Chart.js
    bundle they needed. Both drew numbers that the summary bar and the rows
    already carry — filterable by date and branch, and to the peso rather than
    to the nearest pixel. The notification section at the foot went too:
    notifications have one home, the bell in the topbar.

    THE REPORT ITSELF is views/partials/payment-collection.ejs — the summary,
    the filter bar (search, From/To, branch for the main admin, method, purpose,
    Apply, Clear, Print) and the transactions — because the Payment collection
    tab of Analytics & Reports shows the very same report.

    Locals: rows (every transaction the filters return), summary, filters,
            paymentMethods, paymentPurposes %>
<section class="mq-page">
  <%- include('../partials/payment-collection', {
    rows,
    summary,
    values: typeof filters === 'undefined' ? {} : filters,
    paymentMethods,
    paymentPurposes,
    action: `${basePath}/income-report`,
    names: { search: 'search', from: 'from', to: 'to', branch: 'branch_id', method: 'method', purpose: 'purpose' },
    keep: [],
    clearHref: `${basePath}/income-report`,
    analyticsTab: null,
    showPrint: true,
    headingTag: 'h2'
  }) %>
</section>
